D("pioneer",{etymology:E("From Old French pionnier ‘foot soldier, settler’, based on pion; the noun came to mean an early settler or innovator, and the verb ‘be first to develop or use’ grew from that sense.",null,"pion",null,"Etymonline, pioneer (https://www.etymonline.com/word/pioneer)."),contexts:[C("pioneer.s1","通用","The engineer was a pioneer in low-cost solar storage, developing a design later adopted by several countries.","這位工程師是低成本太陽能儲能領域的先驅，所開發的設計後來被多國採用。","A pioneer is among the first to develop an idea or method.","A pioneer in introduces the field; developing gives evidence of the early work.","The design was new and became a model for others."),C("pioneer.s2","歷史","The pioneers crossed the plains in covered wagons and established a settlement near the river.","拓荒者乘篷車穿越平原，在河邊建立定居點。","A pioneer can be one of the first people to settle in a new area.","Pioneers is the subject; in covered wagons describes their travel.","They move into a region before it is widely settled."),C("pioneer.s3","書面","The hospital pioneered a mobile clinic that brought vaccinations to isolated mountain villages.","這家醫院率先推出行動診所，把疫苗送到偏遠山村。","To pioneer is to be first to do, use, or develop something.","Pioneered takes clinic as object; that-clause describes its service.","The hospital introduces a new model that others may follow.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The institute pioneered the standard method by copying it unchanged after every other laboratory had used it for decades.","The institute adopted the standard method after others had used it; to pioneer a method is to be among its first developers.","Pioneer means lead in introducing something, not merely adopt a long-established approach.")],quiz:[Q("pioneer.q1","pioneer.s1","meaning","A scientific pioneer is someone who ___.",["is among the first to develop a method","only repeats an old method","works as a ship’s cook"],"is among the first to develop a method","The innovator sense describes early development of an idea or method.","meaning"),Q("pioneer.q2","pioneer.s2","context","In a history chapter, pioneers settling a valley are ___.",["among its earliest settlers","the last tourists to leave","people repairing a modern road"],"among its earliest settlers","The historical sense refers to people who settle a new area early.","context"),Q("pioneer.q3","pioneer.s3","grammar","In “The lab pioneered a new test,” pioneered means ___.",["was first to develop or use it","paid someone else to test it","refused to test it"],"was first to develop or use it","The verb means lead in introducing a practice.","grammar"),Q("pioneer.q4","pioneer.s1","word-choice","She became a ____ of bilingual education by designing one of the first programs.",["pioneer","pinhead","pistil"],"pioneer","Her early work makes her an innovator in the field.","word-choice")]});
D("pioneering",{etymology:E("Formed from pioneer + -ing; pioneer came through Old French pionnier, first for an early settler and later for an innovator who opens a path for others.",null,"pioneer","-ing","Etymonline, pioneer (https://www.etymonline.com/word/pioneer)."),contexts:[C("pioneering.s1","通用","The clinic’s pioneering program delivered prenatal care by drone to villages cut off by seasonal floods.","診所開創性的計畫利用無人機，把產前照護送到季節性洪水隔絕的村落。","Pioneering means introducing something for the first time and opening a way for others.","Pioneering modifies program; by drone states its novel method.","The program tests a new way to serve isolated communities.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The company called its pioneering design a copy of a familiar product that had been unchanged for a century.","The company called its new, first-of-its-kind design pioneering because it opened a way for later products.","Pioneering describes an innovative first that leads others, not an unchanged routine copy.")],quiz:[Q("pioneering.q1","pioneering.s1","meaning","A pioneering treatment is ___.",["new and opening a path for later work","an ordinary copy of a familiar method","a treatment that has never been tried and has failed"],"new and opening a path for later work","Pioneering means introducing something new that others can follow.","meaning"),Q("pioneering.q2","pioneering.s1","context","Which project is pioneering?",["The first community-run battery network in the region","A routine copy of last year’s report","A plan that forbids any new approach"],"The first community-run battery network in the region","It introduces a new model that may guide later projects.","context"),Q("pioneering.q3","pioneering.s1","word-choice","The researcher received an award for her ____ work on safer vaccines.",["pioneering","pitiable","pitiless"],"pioneering","Her work opened a new direction for vaccine research.","word-choice"),Q("pioneering.q4","pioneering.s1","meaning","Why can a pioneering method influence later teams?",["It is among the first to show a new way forward.","It prevents anyone from changing an old routine.","It measures the edge of a field."],"It is among the first to show a new way forward.","An innovation can provide a model for subsequent work.","meaning")]});
D("pious",{etymology:E("From Latin pius ‘dutiful, devout’, through Old French; pious describes strong religious belief and practice, and may also imply dutiful respect.",null,"pius",null,"Etymonline, pious (https://www.etymonline.com/word/pious)."),contexts:[C("pious.s1","宗教","The pious family observed the fast together and spent the evening reading prayers at home.","這個虔誠的家庭一起守齋，晚上在家誦讀祈禱文。","Pious means having strong religious belief and practice.","Pious modifies family; observed and spent give examples of practice.","The family’s observances show religious devotion rather than a casual belief.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The pious worshipper rejected every religious practice, mocked prayer, and showed no belief or reverence.","The pious worshipper prayed regularly and showed deep religious belief.","Pious describes religious devotion, the opposite of rejecting all practice and mocking prayer.")],quiz:[Q("pious.q1","pious.s1","meaning","A pious person is ___.",["deeply religious or devout","uninterested in all belief","an expert on plumbing"],"deeply religious or devout","Pious describes strong religious belief and observance.","meaning"),Q("pious.q2","pious.s1","context","Which behavior might be called pious?",["Praying regularly as part of a sincere faith","Mocking every act of worship","Refusing to enter any place of worship for no reason"],"Praying regularly as part of a sincere faith","Regular prayer can show religious devotion.","context"),Q("pious.q3","pious.s1","word-choice","The ____ monk devoted each dawn to prayer and service.",["pious","pinkish","pinpoint"],"pious","The monk’s devotion is the quality described.","word-choice"),Q("pious.q4","pious.s1","meaning","What does a pious routine usually reflect?",["Religious commitment and reverence","An interest in measuring liquids","A new style of roof"],"Religious commitment and reverence","Piety and pious describe devotion in belief and practice.","meaning")]});
D("pip",{etymology:E("The fruit-seed noun is recorded in Middle English; its deeper history is uncertain, and proposed links with related seed words are not conclusive. It names a small hard seed inside fruit such as an apple.",null,null,null,"Etymonline, pip (https://www.etymonline.com/word/pip)."),contexts:[C("pip.s1","飲食","She removed every pip from the lemon before squeezing its juice into the tea.","她把檸檬裡的籽全部取出，再把果汁擠進茶裡。","A pip is a small hard seed found in fruit such as an apple or lemon.","Every pip is the object of removed; before sequences the preparation.","The small seeds are distinct from the juicy flesh of the fruit.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The lemon’s pips were its soft yellow juice, so the cook saved them to sweeten the tea.","The lemon’s pips were its small hard seeds, which the cook removed before squeezing it.","A pip is a seed, not the juice or flesh of a fruit.")],quiz:[Q("pip.q1","pip.s1","meaning","A pip in an apple is ___.",["a small hard seed","a piece of peel","a drop of juice"],"a small hard seed","Pip names a small seed inside some fruits.","meaning"),Q("pip.q2","pip.s1","context","Why might someone remove pips before making lemon juice?",["To keep the seeds out of the drink","To remove the fruit’s color","To stop the juice from being liquid"],"To keep the seeds out of the drink","Pips are seeds that can be removed from the squeezed fruit.","context"),Q("pip.q3","pip.s1","word-choice","The child spat a watermelon ____ into the napkin.",["pip","pinnacle","pilot"],"pip","The small hard seed from the fruit is a pip.","word-choice"),Q("pip.q4","pip.s1","meaning","Which object is a pip?",["A hard seed inside a lemon","A metal tube carrying gas","A small framed notice"],"A hard seed inside a lemon","A pip is a seed from a fruit.","meaning")]});
D("pipe",{etymology:E("From Old English pipe, from Latin pipare ‘chirp, peep’, probably echoing a short sound; the noun extended from a tube or musical pipe to a smoking pipe, and the verb means convey fluid through pipes.",null,"pipare?","-","Etymonline, pipe (https://www.etymonline.com/word/pipe)."),contexts:[C("pipe.s1","生活","A burst pipe flooded the basement before the caretaker could shut off the water.","管理員來得及關水之前，一根爆裂的水管已淹了地下室。","A pipe is a tube through which water, gas, or oil can flow.","A burst pipe is the subject; before marks the delayed response.","The damaged tube carries water into the building."),C("pipe.s2","生活","The shepherd packed his tobacco pipe away before entering the smoke-free train.","牧羊人進入禁菸列車前，把煙斗收了起來。","A pipe can be a narrow tube with a bowl at one end for smoking tobacco.","Tobacco pipe is the object of packed away; before states when.","The context of tobacco and a bowl identifies the smoking implement."),C("pipe.s3","音樂","A high pipe in the organ sustained a clear note throughout the quiet passage.","管風琴中的一根高音音管，在安靜樂段中持續發出清亮音符。","A pipe can be a simple musical tube or one of an organ’s tubes.","A high pipe is the subject; in the organ identifies the instrument.","The pipe produces a musical tone as part of the organ."),C("pipe.s4","工程","The utility plans to pipe natural gas from the coastal terminal to inland factories.","公用事業公司計畫用管線把天然氣從海岸終端輸送到內陸工廠。","To pipe a substance is to send liquid or gas through pipes.","Pipe is a transitive verb with natural gas as object; from and to mark route.","The gas is transported through a connected pipe system.")],mistakes:[M("word-choice","The plumber installed a pipe, a bowl-ended tool used to smoke tobacco, to carry water to the sink.","The plumber installed a water pipe, a tube that carries water to the sink.","For plumbing, a pipe is a fluid-carrying tube; a smoking pipe has a bowl and is a different sense.")],quiz:[Q("pipe.q1","pipe.s1","meaning","A water pipe is ___.",["a tube that carries water","a piece of fruit seed","a bird’s wing"],"a tube that carries water","This is the plumbing sense of the noun.","meaning"),Q("pipe.q2","pipe.s2","context","Which object is a tobacco pipe?",["A narrow stem with a bowl for smoking","A long gas line under a road","An organ’s musical tube"],"A narrow stem with a bowl for smoking","The bowl and tobacco context mark the smoking sense.","context"),Q("pipe.q3","pipe.s3","meaning","An organ pipe is used to ___.",["produce a musical note","carry drinking water to a faucet","store tobacco ash"],"produce a musical note","The musical tube contributes sound to the organ.","meaning"),Q("pipe.q4","pipe.s4","word-choice","The city will ____ treated water to the new housing block.",["pipe","pinch","pioneer"],"pipe","The city will transport water through a pipe system.","word-choice")]});
D("pipefitter",{etymology:E("A compound of pipe + fitter; fitter is an agent noun from fit, describing a tradesperson who installs, joins, and repairs pipe systems.",null,"pipe + fit","-er","Etymonline, fitter (https://www.etymonline.com/word/fitter)."),contexts:[C("pipefitter.s1","職業","The pipefitter replaced the corroded steel joint before the factory restarted its cooling system.","工廠重新啟動冷卻系統前，管道安裝工更換了腐蝕的鋼接頭。","A pipefitter installs and repairs metal pipes.","The pipefitter is the subject; before introduces the repair deadline.","The worker’s trade involves fitting and repairing the facility’s pipes.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The pipefitter repaired the factory’s metal pipes by prescribing medicine to the workers instead of touching the plumbing.","The pipefitter repaired the factory’s metal pipes by replacing the damaged joints.","A pipefitter works on pipe systems; prescribing medicine is a medical task.")],quiz:[Q("pipefitter.q1","pipefitter.s1","meaning","A pipefitter’s job is to ___.",["install and repair pipes","fly passenger aircraft","write musical scores"],"install and repair pipes","The trade centers on fitting metal pipe systems.","meaning"),Q("pipefitter.q2","pipefitter.s1","context","Who should replace a leaking industrial pipe joint?",["A qualified pipefitter","A concert pianist","A fruit seller"],"A qualified pipefitter","Pipefitters install and repair industrial pipes.","context"),Q("pipefitter.q3","pipefitter.s1","word-choice","The contractor hired a ____ to join the new steel water lines.",["pipefitter","pinniped","piety"],"pipefitter","The worker specializes in fitting pipe sections together.","word-choice"),Q("pipefitter.q4","pipefitter.s1","meaning","Why might a pipefitter inspect a welded joint?",["To check that the pipe connection is secure.","To determine whether a bird can fly.","To measure a musician’s pitch."],"To check that the pipe connection is secure.","Secure joints prevent leaks in the pipe system.","meaning")]});
D("pipeline",{etymology:E("A compound of pipe + line, recorded for a line of connected pipes carrying oil, gas, or water; figuratively it can mean a channel through which projects or people progress.",null,"pipe + line",null,"Etymonline, pipeline (https://www.etymonline.com/word/pipeline)."),contexts:[C("pipeline.s1","工業","The new pipeline carries natural gas from the offshore field to the processing plant.","新管線把天然氣從海上氣田輸送到處理廠。","A pipeline is a long connected line of pipes carrying oil, gas, or water.","Pipeline is the subject; from and to identify its route.","The linked tubes transport gas over a long distance.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The pipeline carried natural gas by a row of open buckets that workers passed hand to hand across the sea.","The pipeline carried natural gas through a connected line of pipes from the field to shore.","A pipeline is made of connected pipes that convey the material, not a human bucket chain.")],quiz:[Q("pipeline.q1","pipeline.s1","meaning","An oil pipeline is ___.",["a long connected line of pipes","a single hand-held cup","a type of bird nest"],"a long connected line of pipes","Pipelines transport fluid or gas through joined pipes.","meaning"),Q("pipeline.q2","pipeline.s1","context","Which infrastructure could carry gas across a region?",["A pipeline","A pillow","A painted placard"],"A pipeline","A pipeline carries gas over long distances.","context"),Q("pipeline.q3","pipeline.s1","word-choice","Engineers inspected the ____ for leaks along its route.",["pipeline","pistil","pinprick"],"pipeline","The long pipe network transports the material and must be checked.","word-choice"),Q("pipeline.q4","pipeline.s1","meaning","Why is the word pipeline a compound?",["It combines pipe and line to name a line of pipes.","It combines pillow and pine to name a tree.","It combines pilot and plane to name a person."],"It combines pipe and line to name a line of pipes.","Its parts describe the connected pipe route.","meaning")]});
D("pipes",{etymology:E("The regular plural of pipe; pipe comes from Old English pipe, from Latin pipare ‘chirp, peep’, probably imitative, and names tubes that carry liquids or gases.",null,"pipe / pipare?",null,"Etymonline, pipe (https://www.etymonline.com/word/pipe)."),contexts:[C("pipes.s1","家居","The plumber insulated the pipes beneath the kitchen sink before the first hard freeze.","第一次嚴寒來臨前，水管工為廚房水槽下方的管道加裝了保溫層。","Pipes are tubes that carry water or other liquids.","Pipes is the object of insulated; beneath locates them.","The plural refers to the connected water-carrying tubes under the sink.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The house’s pipes were cushions placed under the residents’ heads, not tubes carrying any liquid.","The house’s pipes were tubes that carried water to the kitchen and bathroom.","In plumbing, pipes are hollow tubes for carrying water or other fluids, not pillows.")],quiz:[Q("pipes.q1","pipes.s1","meaning","In a home, pipes usually carry ___.",["water or other liquids","sleeping pillows","paper notices"],"water or other liquids","Household pipes form part of the plumbing system.","meaning"),Q("pipes.q2","pipes.s1","context","Why insulate water pipes before winter?",["To reduce the risk of freezing","To make them produce music","To turn them into furniture"],"To reduce the risk of freezing","Cold can freeze water in pipes and cause damage.","context"),Q("pipes.q3","pipes.s1","word-choice","The plumber checked the ____ for a leak under the sink.",["pipes","pious","pinnacle"],"pipes","The water-carrying tubes under the sink are pipes.","word-choice"),Q("pipes.q4","pipes.s1","plural","What is the singular form of pipes?",["pipe","pipy","pipe's"],"pipe","Pipes is the regular plural of pipe.","plural")]});
D("pipework",{etymology:E("A compound of pipe + work, naming the network or system of pipes installed in a building, machine, or industrial plant.",null,"pipe + work",null,"Etymonline, pipework (https://www.etymonline.com/word/pipework)."),contexts:[C("pipework.s1","工業","The inspection found corrosion in the boiler room’s pipework, so the heating system was shut down for repairs.","檢查發現鍋爐房的管道系統有腐蝕，因此暖氣系統停機維修。","Pipework is the system of pipes in a building or machine.","Pipework is the object of found; so links the finding to the response.","The damaged network of connected tubes requires repair.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The building’s pipework was its collection of curtains and carpets, with no tubes for water or heating.","The building’s pipework was its network of water and heating pipes.","Pipework means the system of pipes, not soft furnishings.")],quiz:[Q("pipework.q1","pipework.s1","meaning","Pipework refers to ___.",["a system of pipes","a worker’s weekly schedule","a musical performance"],"a system of pipes","The compound names connected plumbing or industrial tubes.","meaning"),Q("pipework.q2","pipework.s1","context","Where would a plumber repair pipework?",["In the building’s water or heating network","On a bird’s wing","Inside a printed magazine"],"In the building’s water or heating network","Pipework is the network through which water or other fluids travel.","context"),Q("pipework.q3","pipework.s1","word-choice","The factory replaced the corroded ____ leading to its boilers.",["pipework","perjury","pinkish"],"pipework","The damaged pipe system needs replacement.","word-choice"),Q("pipework.q4","pipework.s1","meaning","What does extensive pipework suggest about a plant?",["It has a large installed network of pipes.","It grows many trees.","It publishes issues every month."],"It has a large installed network of pipes.","The noun collectively describes the facility’s pipe system.","meaning")]});
D("pique",{etymology:E("From French piquer ‘prick, sting’; the noun developed for resentment from wounded pride, while the verb can mean arouse curiosity or wound someone’s pride.",null,"piquer",null,"Etymonline, pique (https://www.etymonline.com/word/pique)."),contexts:[C("pique.s1","情感","In a fit of pique, the captain resigned after the board rejected her proposal without discussion.","董事會未經討論就否決她的提案後，隊長一氣之下辭職。","Pique is resentment caused by hurt pride.","In a fit of pique gives the emotional cause; after states the trigger.","The abrupt resignation follows wounded pride and anger."),C("pique.s2","通用","The unusual title piqued the journalist’s curiosity, so she requested an interview with the author.","這個不尋常的標題引起記者的好奇，因此她向作者要求採訪。","To pique can mean arouse curiosity or wound someone’s pride.","Piqued takes curiosity as object; so links the interest to the request.","The title stimulates the journalist’s desire to learn more.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The unusual title piqued her curiosity by making her completely uninterested and eager to stop reading.","The unusual title piqued her curiosity by making her want to learn what the story contained.","To pique curiosity is to arouse interest, not eliminate it.")],quiz:[Q("pique.q1","pique.s1","meaning","A person acting in a fit of pique is acting from ___.",["hurt pride and resentment","calm scientific observation","physical hunger only"],"hurt pride and resentment","Pique as a noun means resentment caused by wounded pride.","meaning"),Q("pique.q2","pique.s2","context","A mysterious photograph piqued the detective’s curiosity. The detective ___.",["became interested and wanted to know more","felt sleepy and ignored it","was physically pinched by it"],"became interested and wanted to know more","The verb means stimulate curiosity in this context.","context"),Q("pique.q3","pique.s2","word-choice","The strange sound ____ the child’s interest in the old house.",["piqued","piled","piped"],"piqued","The sound aroused the child’s curiosity.","word-choice"),Q("pique.q4","pique.s1","meaning","Why might a person leave in a pique?",["Wounded pride has made them resentful.","They have just eaten a fruit seed.","They are measuring a liquid."],"Wounded pride has made them resentful.","This noun sense is resentment following an insult or disappointment.","meaning")]});
D("piracy",{etymology:E("From pirate + -cy; pirate comes through Latin pirata from Greek peiratēs ‘brigand, sea robber’, related to peiran ‘attempt, attack’. English piracy covers sea robbery and unauthorized copying of protected works.",null,"peiratēs","-cy","Etymonline, pirate (https://www.etymonline.com/word/pirate)."),contexts:[C("piracy.s1","通用","Naval patrols increased after piracy threatened cargo ships moving through the narrow strait.","海盜行為威脅穿越狹窄海峽的貨船後，海軍加強了巡邏。","Piracy is the crime of attacking and robbing ships at sea.","Piracy is the subject; after introduces the threat that prompted patrols.","Armed attacks on vessels in the strait endanger cargo and crew."),C("piracy.s2","通用","The publisher used digital watermarks to discourage piracy of its new textbook.","出版社使用數位浮水印，防止新教材遭到盜版。","Piracy can mean illegal copying or use of books, music, software, or films.","Piracy is the object of discourage; of its new textbook specifies the work.","Unauthorized copying violates the publisher’s rights.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The publisher called its authorized, licensed sale of every textbook piracy even though each copy had been purchased legally.","The publisher called unauthorized copying and distribution of its textbook piracy.","Copyright piracy is illegal copying or use; a licensed sale is authorized and legal.")],quiz:[Q("piracy.q1","piracy.s1","meaning","At sea, piracy involves ___.",["attacking and robbing ships","repairing a ship’s engine","guiding ships into a port"],"attacking and robbing ships","The maritime sense is robbery or attacks on vessels.","meaning"),Q("piracy.q2","piracy.s2","context","Sharing unauthorized copies of a paid film is ___.",["copyright piracy","safe navigation","piecework"],"copyright piracy","The digital sense is illegal copying or use of protected work.","context"),Q("piracy.q3","piracy.s2","word-choice","The software company pursued a case against online ____ of its program.",["piracy","pinniped","pistil"],"piracy","The case concerns unauthorized copying of software.","word-choice"),Q("piracy.q4","piracy.s1","meaning","Why might patrol boats target piracy?",["It threatens ships and crews with robbery at sea.","It helps every ship find its harbor pilot.","It measures a route’s perimeter."],"It threatens ships and crews with robbery at sea.","Maritime piracy involves attacks and robbery of vessels.","meaning")]});
D("pirate",{etymology:E("From Latin pirata, from Greek peiratēs ‘brigand, sea robber’, related to peiran ‘attempt, attack’; the noun names a sea robber or copyright infringer, and the verb means make unauthorized copies.",null,"peiratēs",null,"Etymonline, pirate (https://www.etymonline.com/word/pirate)."),contexts:[C("pirate.s1","歷史","The pirate crew seized merchant ships in the Caribbean and hid the cargo in a sheltered cove.","海盜船員在加勒比海劫持商船，並把貨物藏在避風灣。","A pirate is a person who attacks and robs ships at sea.","Pirate crew is the subject; in the Caribbean gives the setting.","The crew commits robbery against vessels at sea."),C("pirate.s2","法律","The studio sued a company that sold pirate copies of its films without permission.","片商起訴一家未經許可販售盜版影片的公司。","A pirate can be a person or company that copies works without authorization.","A company that sold introduces the infringing party; without permission establishes the violation.","The copies are unauthorized reproductions of copyrighted films."),C("pirate.s3","法律","Several websites pirated the documentary and offered it for download before its official release.","幾個網站在紀錄片正式上映前就非法複製並提供下載。","To pirate a work is to copy and distribute it without the owner’s permission.","Pirated takes documentary as object; and links copying to distribution.","The sites distribute an unauthorized copy of the film.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The studio praised a pirate company because it copied and sold the films only after receiving written permission from the owners.","The studio praised a licensed distributor because it sold the films with written permission from the owners.","A pirate copies or sells a work without permission; authorized distribution is not piracy.")],quiz:[Q("pirate.q1","pirate.s1","meaning","A historical pirate was a person who ___.",["robbed ships at sea","repaired a harbor wall","measured a sailing route"],"robbed ships at sea","The original common noun sense is a sea robber.","meaning"),Q("pirate.q2","pirate.s2","context","A business selling unlicensed copies of software is a ___.",["pirate","pipefitter","pioneer"],"pirate","The figurative legal sense refers to unauthorized copying.","context"),Q("pirate.q3","pirate.s3","grammar","In “They pirated the film,” pirated means ___.",["copied it without permission","reviewed it legally","showed it to the director"],"copied it without permission","The verb describes unauthorized copying or distribution.","grammar"),Q("pirate.q4","pirate.s1","word-choice","The merchant ship hired guards to deter ____ attacks at sea.",["pirate","pious","pinkish"],"pirate","The guards protect the ship from sea robbers.","word-choice")]});
D("piscatorial",{etymology:E("From Latin piscatorius ‘of a fisherman’, from piscator ‘fisherman’, based on piscis ‘fish’; the adjective relates to fishermen, fishing, or fish.",null,"piscis","-atorial","Etymonline, piscatorial (https://www.etymonline.com/word/piscatorial)."),contexts:[C("piscatorial.s1","生活","The novel’s piscatorial details—bait, tide tables, and a battered tackle box—show the author knows fishing firsthand.","小說裡關於魚餌、潮汐表和舊釣具箱的漁業細節，顯示作者熟悉捕魚。","Piscatorial means relating to fishermen or the occupation of fishing.","Piscatorial modifies details; the dash introduces examples of them.","The listed equipment and methods belong to fishing life.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The piscatorial chapter described mountain climbing equipment and never mentioned fish, fishermen, or fishing.","The piscatorial chapter described fishing gear, fish, and the work of fishermen.","Piscatorial relates to fish or fishing; mountaineering alone is outside the adjective’s meaning.")],quiz:[Q("piscatorial.q1","piscatorial.s1","meaning","A piscatorial book concerns ___.",["fishing or fishermen","aircraft design","flower reproduction"],"fishing or fishermen","The adjective means connected with fishing or fishers.","meaning"),Q("piscatorial.q2","piscatorial.s1","context","Which detail is piscatorial?",["A chart of tides used by a fishing crew","A pilot’s flight checklist","A painter’s color palette"],"A chart of tides used by a fishing crew","Tide tables used for fishing fit the adjective.","context"),Q("piscatorial.q3","piscatorial.s1","word-choice","The memoir is full of ____ stories about life on fishing boats.",["piscatorial","pitiable","perilous"],"piscatorial","The stories concern fishermen and their occupation.","word-choice"),Q("piscatorial.q4","piscatorial.s1","word-formation","The Latin root piscis means ___.",["fish","stone","feather"],"fish","Piscatorial is based on the Latin word for fish.","word-formation")]});
D("pistachio",{etymology:E("From Italian pistacchio and Latin pistacium, from Greek pistakion, ultimately from a Persian word for the nut; English names both the tree and its beige-shelled green kernel.",null,"Persian pistah (ultimate source)",null,"Etymonline, pistachio (https://www.etymonline.com/word/pistachio)."),contexts:[C("pistachio.s1","飲食","He crushed pistachios over the rice pudding, adding a green crunch and a mild nutty flavor.","他把開心果壓碎撒在米布丁上，增添綠色脆感和淡淡堅果香。","A pistachio is a nut with a beige shell and green kernel, or the tree that bears it.","Pistachios is the object of crushed; over gives their position on the dessert.","The green kernels are edible nuts from the pistachio tree.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The baker added pistachios, bright red berries with blue shells and no edible kernel, to the pudding.","The baker added pistachios, beige-shelled nuts with green kernels, to the pudding.","Pistachios are nuts with beige shells and green kernels, not red berries.")],quiz:[Q("pistachio.q1","pistachio.s1","meaning","A pistachio kernel is commonly ___.",["green inside a beige shell","blue inside a red shell","a long black feather"],"green inside a beige shell","The nut’s characteristic shell and kernel are beige and green.","meaning"),Q("pistachio.q2","pistachio.s1","context","Which dish might be topped with crushed pistachios?",["Rice pudding","A steel pipe","A paper map"],"Rice pudding","Pistachios are edible nuts commonly used as a topping.","context"),Q("pistachio.q3","pistachio.s1","word-choice","The ice cream was flavored with roasted ____ nuts.",["pistachio","pinniped","pistil"],"pistachio","Pistachio nuts give the dessert their distinctive flavor.","word-choice"),Q("pistachio.q4","pistachio.s1","meaning","What part of a pistachio tree is eaten as a snack?",["Its nut or seed kernel","Its metal trunk","Its flower’s root system"],"Its nut or seed kernel","The edible pistachio is the nut produced by the tree.","meaning")]});
D("pistil",{etymology:E("From Latin pistillum ‘pestle’, a small crushing tool; the botanical term was applied to the central seed-bearing flower structure, whose shape was likened to a pestle.",null,"pistillum",null,"Etymonline, pistil (https://www.etymonline.com/word/pistil)."),contexts:[C("pistil.s1","植物","The botanist pointed out the pistil at the center of the lily, including its stigma, style, and ovary.","植物學家指出百合花中央的雌蕊，包括柱頭、花柱和子房。","A pistil is a flower’s seed-bearing structure, usually including stigma, style, and ovary.","Pistil is the object of pointed out; including lists its parts.","The structure receives pollen and contains the ovary that can develop seeds.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The flower’s pistil was its outer green leaf, which carried no reproductive parts and grew on the tree trunk.","The flower’s pistil was its seed-bearing central structure, including the stigma and ovary.","A pistil is the female reproductive structure of a flower, not an outer leaf.")],quiz:[Q("pistil.q1","pistil.s1","meaning","A flower’s pistil is its ___.",["seed-bearing structure","outer bark","root hair"],"seed-bearing structure","The pistil is the female reproductive part of the flower.","meaning"),Q("pistil.q2","pistil.s1","context","Which parts may belong to a pistil?",["Stigma, style, and ovary","Petal, bark, and trunk","Needle, cone, and root"],"Stigma, style, and ovary","Those structures are commonly parts of a flower’s pistil.","context"),Q("pistil.q3","pistil.s1","word-choice","Pollen reaches the ____ of a flower during reproduction.",["pistil","pillow","pipeline"],"pistil","The female seed-bearing structure receives pollen.","word-choice"),Q("pistil.q4","pistil.s1","meaning","Why is the ovary part of a pistil important?",["It can develop seeds after fertilization.","It carries water through a building.","It produces a musical note."],"It can develop seeds after fertilization.","The pistil contains the flower’s ovary, where seeds develop.","meaning")]});
D("pistol",{etymology:E("From French pistole and Italian pistola; the ultimate source is uncertain, with proposals linking it to a Czech word for a small firearm or to a place-name. The modern noun is a handgun.",null,"pistola (ultimate origin uncertain)",null,"Etymonline, pistol (https://www.etymonline.com/word/pistol)."),contexts:[C("pistol.s1","武器","The museum displayed an antique pistol behind glass, with a notice explaining its history and safe handling.","博物館把一把古董手槍陳列在玻璃櫃中，並附上歷史與安全處理說明。","A pistol is a small firearm designed to be used with one hand.","Pistol is the object of displayed; behind glass specifies its protected position.","The exhibit identifies a handheld firearm, secured for museum visitors."),C("pistol.s2","體育","The starter fired a starting pistol, and the runners left the blocks at the signal.","發令員鳴響發令槍，跑者聽到訊號後從起跑器衝出。","A pistol can be a hand gun used to start a race or send a signal.","Starting pistol identifies its use; and links signal to the runners’ response.","The sound signals the start rather than serving as an attack.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","At the track meet, the starter used a starting pistol to hand each runner a written map without making a sound.","At the track meet, the starter fired a starting pistol to give the runners an audible signal.","A starting pistol signals a race with a sound; it is not a silent paper-distribution tool.")],quiz:[Q("pistol.q1","pistol.s1","meaning","A pistol is a firearm usually designed to be used ___.",["with one hand","only by mounting it on a ship","as a piece of clothing"],"with one hand","A pistol is a small hand-held firearm.","meaning"),Q("pistol.q2","pistol.s2","context","Why might an official fire a starting pistol at a race?",["To signal that the runners should start","To measure the track’s length","To award a trophy"],"To signal that the runners should start","A starting pistol produces the race-start signal.","context"),Q("pistol.q3","pistol.s1","word-choice","The historical exhibit showed a one-handed ____ in a locked case.",["pistol","pistil","pint"],"pistol","The object is a small handheld firearm.","word-choice"),Q("pistol.q4","pistol.s2","meaning","In the phrase starting pistol, what is its role?",["It provides a signal to begin.","It holds liquid for the runners.","It marks the race’s finish line."],"It provides a signal to begin.","The narrow sports sense is a gun used to signal a start.","meaning")]});
D("piston",{etymology:E("From French piston, from Italian pistone ‘large pestle’, related to Latin pinsere ‘pound’; the mechanical part slides inside a cylinder, and the word also names a sliding valve on some brass instruments.",null,"pinsere?","-","Etymonline, piston (https://www.etymonline.com/word/piston)."),contexts:[C("piston.s1","通用","Combustion pushed the engine’s piston down inside the cylinder, turning the crankshaft.","燃燒推動發動機活塞在汽缸內下行，帶動曲軸轉動。","A piston is a round metal part that slides inside an engine.","Piston is the object of pushed; down inside locates its motion.","The moving part transfers force from the expanding gas to the crankshaft."),C("piston.s2","音樂","The trumpet player pressed the second piston to lower the note during the passage.","小號手在樂段中按下第二個活塞閥鍵，降低音高。","A piston can be a sliding valve on a trumpet that changes the note.","Second piston is the object of pressed; to lower states its musical effect.","The valve changes the tube length and therefore the pitch.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The trumpet’s piston changed the note by sliding inside a car engine cylinder, while the mechanic played the melody.","The trumpet’s piston valve changed the note when the musician pressed it.","In a trumpet, piston means a sliding valve that changes pitch, not an engine part.")],quiz:[Q("piston.q1","piston.s1","meaning","An engine piston moves inside a ___.",["cylinder","flower petal","glass of water"],"cylinder","The piston slides up and down inside an engine cylinder.","meaning"),Q("piston.q2","piston.s2","context","What does a trumpet piston help the player do?",["Change the note","Fuel the engine","Measure the instrument’s weight"],"Change the note","The sliding valve changes the trumpet’s pitch.","context"),Q("piston.q3","piston.s1","word-choice","The mechanic replaced a worn ____ inside the car’s cylinder.",["piston","piety","pioneer"],"piston","The engine component slides inside the cylinder.","word-choice"),Q("piston.q4","piston.s2","meaning","Why does pressing a trumpet piston alter the sound?",["It changes the air path and pitch.","It squeezes a fruit seed.","It paints the trumpet pink."],"It changes the air path and pitch.","The valve redirects air to change the note.","meaning")]});
D("pit",{etymology:E("From Old English pytt ‘pit, hole’, from Latin puteus ‘well, shaft’; the fruit-stone sense is a separate use, and the verb pit against means set one person or thing in opposition to another.",null,"puteus (pit sense)",null,"Etymonline, pit (https://www.etymonline.com/word/pit)."),contexts:[C("pit.s1","通用","The workers fenced off a deep pit where the old foundation had been removed.","工人把舊地基移除後留下的深坑圍了起來。","A pit is a large, deep hole in the ground.","Pit is the object of fenced off; where gives its location.","The excavation leaves a dangerous open hole in the ground."),C("pit.s2","工業","His grandfather worked in a coal pit in northern England before the mine closed.","礦場關閉前，他的祖父曾在英格蘭北部的煤礦工作。","In British English, a pit can mean a coal mine.","Coal pit is the object of worked in; before marks the mine’s closure.","The word refers to the underground mining workplace."),C("pit.s3","飲食","She removed the cherry pit before giving the fruit to the young child.","她把櫻桃核取出後才把水果交給年幼的孩子。","A pit is the hard stone in the middle of some fruits.","Cherry pit is the object of removed; before gives the order of actions.","The hard seed casing in the fruit must be removed before eating."),C("pit.s4","通用","The tournament will pit the reigning champion against a fast-rising newcomer.","這場錦標賽將讓衛冕冠軍與迅速崛起的新秀對決。","To pit one person or thing against another is to make them compete or oppose each other.","Pit takes champion as object and against introduces the opponent.","The tournament arranges a direct competition between them.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The tournament pitted the two teams together as close friends who never competed against each other.","The tournament pitted the two teams against each other in a direct competition.","To pit A against B means set them in competition, not simply make them companions.")],quiz:[Q("pit.q1","pit.s1","meaning","A construction pit is ___.",["a deep hole in the ground","a soft cloth head support","a musical composition"],"a deep hole in the ground","This is the excavation sense of pit.","meaning"),Q("pit.q2","pit.s2","context","In a British history book, a miner worked in a pit. Where did the person work?",["A coal mine","A fruit orchard","A theater stage"],"A coal mine","Pit is a British term for a coal mine.","context"),Q("pit.q3","pit.s3","meaning","A cherry pit is ___.",["the hard stone inside the fruit","a large hole in a road","a type of fish"],"the hard stone inside the fruit","The fruit sense names its hard central stone.","meaning"),Q("pit.q4","pit.s4","word-choice","The final match will ____ the veteran against the rookie.",["pit","pillow","pioneer"],"pit","The verb means arrange for them to compete against one another.","word-choice")]});
D("pitch",{etymology:E("Pitch has several histories: the throwing verb is probably from Old English piccean ‘thrust’; musical pitch is from Old French pitch/pech (resin or tar) with a later sound sense; the sports field sense comes from a place marked or pitched. Histories are not all one root.",null,"piccean / Old French pic","-","Etymonline, pitch (https://www.etymonline.com/word/pitch)."),contexts:[C("pitch.s1","通用","He pitched the tent beside the stream before the temperature dropped after sunset.","日落後氣溫下降前，他在溪邊搭起了帳篷。","To pitch can mean throw something with force or put up a tent.","Pitched takes tent as object; beside gives its site.","Here the verb means set up camp, not throw a tent."),C("pitch.s2","音樂","The oboe sounded a steady pitch so the orchestra could tune before the concert.","雙簧管奏出穩定音高，讓管弦樂團在音樂會前調音。","Pitch is how high or low a sound is, or the level of an activity or feeling.","A steady pitch is the object of sounded; so introduces its purpose.","The orchestra matches the height of the musical tone."),C("pitch.s3","體育","The teams returned to the football pitch after halftime to finish the match.","中場休息後，兩隊回到足球場繼續比賽。","In British English, a pitch is a marked area of ground used for sport.","Football pitch is the object of returned to; after marks the time.","The players resume the game on its playing field."),C("pitch.s4","通用","Her sales pitch emphasized the repair service’s low cost and two-year guarantee.","她的推銷說詞強調維修服務價格低廉，並提供兩年保固。","A pitch can be a talk intended to sell an idea or product; it can also mean tar.","Sales pitch is the subject; emphasized states its main points.","The speaker is persuading potential customers rather than describing a sound.")],mistakes:[M("word-choice","The orchestra tuned its pitch by running onto the football field and kicking the ball between notes.","The orchestra matched its pitch by adjusting the highness or lowness of its notes.","Musical pitch is sound height; a football pitch is a playing field, a different sense.")],quiz:[Q("pitch.q1","pitch.s1","meaning","To pitch a tent means to ___.",["set it up at a campsite","throw it into a lake","measure its musical note"],"set it up at a campsite","Pitch has a camping sense meaning put up a tent.","meaning"),Q("pitch.q2","pitch.s2","context","A singer changes the pitch of a note by changing its ___.",["highness or lowness","color","weight"],"highness or lowness","Musical pitch describes how high or low a sound is.","context"),Q("pitch.q3","pitch.s3","meaning","In British sports reporting, the pitch is ___.",["the marked playing field","a sales speech","a measurement of loudness only"],"the marked playing field","The sports sense names the field on which the game is played.","meaning"),Q("pitch.q4","pitch.s4","word-choice","The consultant gave a persuasive ____ for her new design.",["pitch","pistil","pint"],"pitch","A pitch can be a talk intended to sell an idea.","word-choice")]});
D("pitched",{etymology:E("Past participle of pitch; the roof adjective means sloping, from the idea of setting or raising a roof, while pitched battle means a deliberately arranged, set-piece engagement. The senses are distinct extensions.",null,"pitch","-ed","Etymonline, pitch (https://www.etymonline.com/word/pitch)."),contexts:[C("pitched.s1","通用","The cabin has a steeply pitched roof that sheds heavy snow before it can accumulate.","小屋的屋頂坡度很陡，能在積雪過多前讓大雪滑落。","A pitched roof is sloping rather than flat.","Pitched modifies roof; that-clause explains the practical effect.","The roof’s incline lets snow slide off."),C("pitched.s2","音樂","The choir began with a clearly pitched note that gave every singer a reliable starting tone.","合唱團以一個音高清楚的音符開始，讓每位歌手都有可靠的起始音。","Pitched can mean having a definite musical pitch.","Pitched modifies note; that-clause explains its use to the singers.","The note has a clear height that singers can match.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The cabin had a flat pitched roof with no slope at all, so rain and snow could not run off.","The cabin had a pitched roof with a clear slope, so rain and snow could run off.","A pitched roof is sloping, not flat.")],quiz:[Q("pitched.q1","pitched.s1","meaning","A pitched roof is ___.",["sloping","completely flat","made only of glass"],"sloping","This adjective sense describes a roof with an incline.","meaning"),Q("pitched.q2","pitched.s2","context","A clearly pitched note helps a choir because it ___.",["has a definite musical height","is a roof that sheds rain","is a field for soccer"],"has a definite musical height","The musical sense concerns a definite pitch a singer can match.","context"),Q("pitched.q3","pitched.s1","word-choice","Snow slides off the barn’s steeply ____ roof.",["pitched","pitiful","pious"],"pitched","The roof slopes enough for snow to slide away.","word-choice"),Q("pitched.q4","pitched.s2","meaning","What does a well-pitched opening note give singers?",["A clear tone to match","A place to stand on the field","A tool for fastening cloth"],"A clear tone to match","A pitched musical note has a definite height.","meaning")]});
